+# Flag Counting Level 19 — Multi-Timeframe State Gate and Dashboard Specification
+
+Status: design specification
+Scope: read-only state projection layer above the locked Phoenix anatomy engines
+Primary implementation target: `FlagCountingPhoenixExperiment.mq5` + `mql5/Include/FlagCountingPhoenix/`
+
+---
+
+## 1. Purpose
+
+Level 19 introduces a live **State Gate** for the Flag Counting project.
+
+This layer is not a new counting engine, not a new rally detector, not a new hook detector, and not an entry system. It is a higher-level state map that reads the already locked Phoenix anatomy outputs and stores the current market position across multiple timeframes from two internal views:
+
+```text
+Rally View = the existing F-counting anatomy projected as live rally-state information.
+Hook View  = the existing Hook/ND and node-count anatomy projected as live hook-state information.
+```
+
+The State Gate is the bridge between anatomy and future entry design. It must hold the current state of the market in memory and render a compact dashboard so that the operator can see, debug, and reason about the structure without changing the locked Node/ND/Hook/F-counting logic.
+
+The design goal is:
+
+```text
+For each selected timeframe, show where price is now inside the existing F anatomy and Hook/ND anatomy.
+```
+
+This creates a live map such as:
+
+```text
+M1  | Rally View | Latest established F2 | probable F3 stage: IN_FLAG / LEG2_BEFORE_LEG1_BREAK
+M1  | Hook View  | L34 positive hook | current node: N2 | latest high node: ... | latest low node: ...
+M10 | Rally View | Latest established F1 | probable F2 stage: POST_FLAG / AFTER_1_BEFORE_2
+H1  | Hook View  | L55 negative hook | current node: N1 | sequence: ...
+```
+
+No buy/sell label is allowed in Level 19. The layer only stores and displays state.
+
+---
+
+## 2. Non-negotiable boundaries
+
+The following engines are locked and must not be changed by Level 19:
+
+```text
+Node / L-rule / scale logic
+Hook / ND logic
+Flag body logic
+Internal count logic
+F1 / F2 / F3 lifecycle logic
+Ownership / canonicalization logic
+Renderer logic
+Validation / release / license gates
+```
+
+Level 19 is a read-only projection layer.
+
+It may:
+
+```text
+read canonical events
+read hook contexts
+read node contexts
+read sequence ownership fields
+read lifecycle status fields
+read current closed-bar price per configured timeframe
+store a derived snapshot
+render a dashboard panel
+export CSV snapshots
+print audit lines
+```
+
+It must not:
+
+```text
+create new nodes
+repair nodes
+change Hook/ND states
+change F states
+hide or unhide events
+promote or demote canonical events
+change sequence ownership
+change the renderer's structural output
+produce entry labels
+produce buy/sell labels
+mutate Phoenix counting state
+```
+
+This is the governing rule:
+
+```text
+Level 19 observes Phoenix anatomy. It never rewrites Phoenix anatomy.
+```
+
+---
+
+## 3. Cadence
+
+The State Gate updates only when a configured timeframe closes a candle.
+
+The default update basis is:
+
+```text
+closed candle only
+```
+
+This means the dashboard is not driven by every tick. It updates when the selected timeframe has a newly closed bar. This prevents unstable intra-candle labels and keeps the state map aligned with the locked anatomy logic.
+
+The implementation must track the latest processed closed-bar time for each configured timeframe.
+
+Example:
+
+```text
+InpStateGateTf1 = PERIOD_M1
+InpStateGateTf2 = PERIOD_M10
+InpStateGateTf3 = PERIOD_H1
+```
+
+The M1 state may update every minute, M10 every ten minutes, and H1 every hour. The panel may redraw after any of the three states updates, but the underlying state row for each timeframe must indicate its own last closed-bar time.
+
+---
+
+## 4. Symbol scope
+
+Level 19 is single-symbol by design.
+
+The symbol is the chart symbol where the EA is attached:
+
+```text
+_state_symbol = _Symbol
+```
+
+No cross-symbol state map is introduced in Level 19.
+
+---
+
+## 5. Timeframe inputs
+
+The State Gate must expose three configurable timeframe inputs.
+
+Default values:
+
+```text
+InpStateGateTf1 = PERIOD_M1
+InpStateGateTf2 = PERIOD_M10
+InpStateGateTf3 = PERIOD_H1
+```
+
+The defaults match the working research map:
+
+```text
+fast view   = 1 minute
+middle view = 10 minutes
+large view  = 1 hour
+```
+
+The implementation may support disabling a timeframe by setting it to `PERIOD_CURRENT` only if the chart timeframe behavior is explicitly documented. Otherwise, all three inputs should be treated as active.
+
+---
+
+## 6. Dashboard role
+
+The dashboard is the visual surface of the State Gate, not the State Gate itself.
+
+The underlying layer must store state even if the dashboard is disabled or minimized. The dashboard exists for:
+
+```text
+visual debugging
+idea development
+operator situational awareness
+checking whether the anatomy-to-entry bridge is reading the right structures
+```
+
+The dashboard must be:
+
+```text
+minimal
+readable
+organized
+right-top corner by default
+collapsible / minimizable
+non-invasive on the chart
+```
+
+Default placement:
+
+```text
+corner: top-right
+x offset: small positive margin
+y offset: small positive margin
+```
+
+The dashboard should have a small title bar with a minimize/restore control.
+
+When minimized, it should show only a compact header, for example:
+
+```text
+FLAG STATE GATE  [M1/M10/H1]  ▣
+```
+
+When expanded, it should show timeframe blocks with Rally View and Hook View rows.
+
+---
+
+## 7. Dashboard inputs
+
+Recommended Level 19 inputs:
+
+```text
+input bool            InpStateGateEnabled              = true;
+input ENUM_TIMEFRAMES InpStateGateTf1                  = PERIOD_M1;
+input ENUM_TIMEFRAMES InpStateGateTf2                  = PERIOD_M10;
+input ENUM_TIMEFRAMES InpStateGateTf3                  = PERIOD_H1;
+
+input bool            InpStateGatePanelEnabled         = true;
+input bool            InpStateGatePanelStartMinimized  = false;
+input int             InpStateGatePanelCorner          = CORNER_RIGHT_UPPER;
+input int             InpStateGatePanelX               = 16;
+input int             InpStateGatePanelY               = 24;
+input int             InpStateGatePanelWidth           = 520;
+input int             InpStateGatePanelFontSize        = 8;
+input int             InpStateGateMaxRallyRowsPerTf    = 6;
+input int             InpStateGateMaxHookRowsPerTf     = 10;
+input bool            InpStateGateShowIds              = true;
+input bool            InpStateGateShowScaleL           = true;
+input bool            InpStateGateExportCsv            = true;
+input bool            InpStateGatePrintAudit           = true;
+```
+
+The final input names may be adjusted to match Phoenix naming style, but the behavior must remain the same.
+
+---
+
+## 8. Core State Gate data model
+
+Level 19 should introduce explicit state structures. Names are proposed, not mandatory.
+
+### 8.1 Snapshot
+
+```text
+FP_StateGateSnapshot
+  symbol
+  generated_at_server_time
+  chart_timeframe
+  row_count
+  tf_state[3]
+```
+
+### 8.2 Timeframe state
+
+```text
+FP_StateGateTimeframeState
+  timeframe
+  last_closed_bar_time
+  last_closed_bar_close
+  rally_row_count
+  hook_row_count
+  latest_established_f_summary
+  probable_next_f_summary
+  hook_summary
+```
+
+### 8.3 Rally row
+
+```text
+FP_StateGateRallyRow
+  symbol
+  timeframe
+  scale_L
+  direction
+  sequence_id
+  event_id
+  canonical_id
+  phase_id
+  chain_id
+  f_level
+  established_f_level
+  probable_next_f_level
+  macro_state
+  flag_stage
+  post_flag_stage
+  leg2_relation
+  current_status
+  source_status
+  source_lifecycle_status
+  last_closed_bar_time
+  last_closed_bar_price
+```
+
+### 8.4 Hook row
+
+```text
+FP_StateGateHookRow
+  symbol
+  timeframe
+  scale_L
+  hook_id
+  sequence_id
+  direction
+  polarity
+  is_nd
+  is_open_or_relevant
+  current_node_number
+  latest_confirmed_node_number
+  latest_high_node_id
+  latest_high_node_price
+  latest_low_node_id
+  latest_low_node_price
+  price_position_label
+  source_hook_status
+  last_closed_bar_time
+  last_closed_bar_price
+```
+
+---
+
+## 9. Rally View semantics
+
+Rally View is not a separate rally classifier. It is the live projection of existing F-counting outputs.
+
+The project does not need a separate `RallyEngine` for Level 19. When the dashboard reads F-counting state, it is already reading the market from the rally perspective.
+
+Therefore:
+
+```text
+Rally View = where price is now inside the existing F anatomy.
+```
+
+Level 19 must show:
+
+```text
+1. The latest established F, up to F3.
+2. The probable next F stage, up to F3.
+3. The sequence identity where the F state belongs.
+4. The current sub-state inside the probable F.
+```
+
+No F4+ logic is introduced in Level 19.
+
+Maximum F level:
+
+```text
+F1
+F2
+F3
+```
+
+If the existing engine internally reports extension/lock after F3, Level 19 may display that as a status note, but it must not introduce new F4/F5 labels.
+
+---
+
+## 10. Latest established F
+
+For each timeframe and relevant sequence, Level 19 must identify the latest established F level.
+
+The label should be one of:
+
+```text
+ESTABLISHED_NONE
+ESTABLISHED_F1
+ESTABLISHED_F2
+ESTABLISHED_F3
+```
+
+The source must be existing Phoenix lifecycle fields.
+
+Level 19 does not decide that an F is established by itself. It reads the locked F lifecycle output and translates it into a dashboard label.
+
+---
+
+## 11. Probable next F stage
+
+After the latest established F, Level 19 should show where price appears to be inside the next probable F anatomy, using the same locked underlying fields and partial body/internal-count state.
+
+Example:
+
+```text
+latest established F = F1
+probable next F = F2
+probable stage = IN_FLAG / LEG2_BEFORE_LEG1_BREAK
+```
+
+This is not a trading prediction. It is a state label for the current anatomy.
+
+---
+
+## 12. Rally macro-states
+
+Each Rally row must use one macro-state:
+
+```text
+IN_FLAG_BODY
+POST_FLAG_BODY
+F_ESTABLISHED
+F_INVALID
+F_LOCKED
+UNKNOWN
+```
+
+The preferred dashboard wording may be shorter:
+
+```text
+IN FLAG
+POST FLAG
+ESTABLISHED
+INVALID
+LOCKED
+UNKNOWN
+```
+
+---
+
+## 13. IN_FLAG_BODY sub-states
+
+When a probable F is still inside its flag body, Level 19 must classify the current body stage as one of:
+
+```text
+PROBABLE_LEG1
+LEG1_CORRECTION
+PROBABLE_LEG2_BEFORE_LEG1_BREAK
+PROBABLE_LEG2_AFTER_LEG1_BREAK
+UNKNOWN_FLAG_STAGE
+```
+
+Definitions:
+
+### PROBABLE_LEG1
+
+Price is inside the early leg that may become the first leg of the probable flag body.
+
+### LEG1_CORRECTION
+
+Price is inside the correction/retracement after the probable first leg and before the probable second leg is structurally active.
+
+### PROBABLE_LEG2_BEFORE_LEG1_BREAK
+
+Price is inside the probable second leg, but the probable second leg has not yet passed the prior leg's extreme in the favorable direction.
+
+### PROBABLE_LEG2_AFTER_LEG1_BREAK
+
+Price is inside the probable second leg and has passed the prior leg's extreme in the favorable direction.
+
+For an up-direction F, the favorable pass is above the relevant prior leg extreme. For a down-direction F, the favorable pass is below the relevant prior leg extreme.
+
+The exact source level must come from the locked Flag Body / F lifecycle engine. Level 19 only labels the relation.
+
+---
+
+## 14. POST_FLAG_BODY sub-states
+
+When the probable F has completed its two-leg flag body and price is now in the post-flag counting region, Level 19 must classify the current post-flag stage as one of:
+
+```text
+BEFORE_1
+AFTER_1_BEFORE_2
+AFTER_2_BEFORE_3
+AFTER_3_BEFORE_4
+AFTER_4_PLUS
+UNKNOWN_POST_FLAG_STAGE
+```
+
+These numbers refer to the post-flag internal count state already produced by Phoenix.
+
+Important distinction:
+
+```text
+Node-counting and F-counting are not the same thing.
+```
+
+The post-flag numbers in Rally View are not raw Hook node numbers. They are part of the F-counting view of the probable next F sequence.
+
+---
+
+## 15. F establishment
+
+The operator rule is:
+
+```text
+An F becomes established when price passes its flag in the favorable direction according to the locked Phoenix F lifecycle logic.
+```
+
+Level 19 must not invent a new establishment rule.
+
+It should display the result as:
+
+```text
+F_ESTABLISHED_BY_FLAG_PASS
+```
+
+or a compact dashboard label:
+
+```text
+ESTABLISHED
+```
+
+The source fields must be the existing F lifecycle status fields.
+
+---
+
+## 16. Hook View semantics
+
+Hook View is the live projection of existing Hook/ND and node-count anatomy.
+
+The project does not need a separate hook phase detector in Level 19. When the dashboard reads Hook/ND contexts and node-count state, it is reading the market from the hook perspective.
+
+Therefore:
+
+```text
+Hook View = where price is now inside all relevant open/relevant Hook/ND cycles across the configured L scales.
+```
+
+Hook View must list the latest status of all relevant hooks from large to small scale.
+
+The source of scale is the existing L sequence:
+
+```text
+L2, L3, L5, L8, L13, L21, L34, L55, ...
+```
+
+The actual available list is whatever the current Phoenix input configuration uses.
+
+---
+
+## 17. Open/relevant Hook definition
+
+A Hook row is eligible for the State Gate if it is still relevant to the latest closed candle.
+
+For Level 19, relevant means:
+
+```text
+A Hook/ND cycle that can still define the current latest high node, latest low node, current node number, or current structural position at its scale.
+```
+
+This intentionally includes multiple nested hooks across the L sequence.
+
+The dashboard is expected to show a long list if many hooks are relevant. This is part of the anatomy map, not a bug.
+
+The panel may cap visible rows with `InpStateGateMaxHookRowsPerTf`, but the internal State Gate snapshot and CSV export should preserve the full relevant list unless export limits are explicitly configured.
+
+---
+
+## 18. Hook polarity
+
+Hook polarity must be displayed.
+
+The project-specific polarity definition is:
+
+```text
+Positive Hook = the semi-circle structure whose terminal side points downward; if it reverses, the reverse direction is upward.
+Negative Hook = the inverse structure whose terminal side points upward; if it reverses, the reverse direction is downward.
+```
+
+Dashboard labels:
+
+```text
+HOOK+
+HOOK-
+ND+
+ND-
+```
+
+Positive and negative labels are state labels only. They are not entry instructions.
+
+---
+
+## 19. Hook node state
+
+For each Hook row, Level 19 must show:
+
+```text
+hook id
+sequence id
+scale L
+polarity
+ND or non-ND
+latest confirmed node number
+current node number / current node position
+latest confirmed high node id and price
+latest confirmed low node id and price
+price position label
+```
+
+Example dashboard row:
+
+```text
+L34 | HOOK+ | H#148 | Seq#42 | N2 | Hi:N771 @ 2368.2 | Lo:N769 @ 2351.4
+```
+
+Another example:
+
+```text
+L13 | ND- | H#151 | Seq#44 | N3 | price: BETWEEN_N2_N3
+```
+
+---
+
+## 20. Price position labels for Hook View
+
+Recommended Hook position labels:
+
+```text
+BEFORE_N1
+AT_N1
+BETWEEN_N1_N2
+AT_N2
+BETWEEN_N2_N3
+AT_N3
+BETWEEN_N3_N4
+AT_N4
+AFTER_N4
+UNKNOWN_HOOK_POSITION
+```
+
+If Phoenix only has enough data to identify the latest confirmed node number and not a precise between-node relation, Level 19 may initially report:
+
+```text
+CURRENT_NODE_N1
+CURRENT_NODE_N2
+CURRENT_NODE_N3
+CURRENT_NODE_N4_PLUS
+```
+
+and later upgrade to between-node labels.
+
+---
+
+## 21. Dashboard layout
+
+The panel should be compact and readable.
+
+Recommended expanded layout:
+
+```text
+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
+│ FLAG STATE GATE   GOLD   closed-bar   [M1/M10/H1]        [-] │
+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
+│ M1  last close: 2026.xx.xx 12:34  price: 2361.20            │
+│  Rally: latest F2 | next F3 | IN FLAG | LEG2 BEFORE BREAK   │
+│          Seq#102 Chain#55 Ev#881 L13                         │
+│  Hook:  L55 HOOK+ H#44 Seq#17 N2 Hi#... Lo#...               │
+│         L34 ND-   H#45 Seq#18 N1 Hi#... Lo#...               │
+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
+│ M10 last close: ...                                          │
+│  Rally: latest F1 | next F2 | POST FLAG | AFTER_1_BEFORE_2   │
+│  Hook:  ...                                                  │
+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
+│ H1  last close: ...                                          │
+│  Rally: ...                                                  │
+│  Hook:  ...                                                  │
+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
+```
+
+If the row list is too long, the panel may show top rows and add a compact continuation note:
+
+```text
++ 7 more hook rows in CSV
+```
+
+The dashboard must never become more important than chart readability.
+
+---
+
