+```
+
+The CSV export is critical for debugging the future anatomy-to-entry bridge.
+
+---
+
+## 23. Audit logging
+
+When enabled, Level 19 should print compact audit lines:
+
+```text
+FP_LEVEL19_STATE_GATE symbol=GOLD tf=M1 close_time=... rally_rows=... hook_rows=...
+FP_LEVEL19_RALLY tf=M1 seq=... established=F2 next=F3 macro=IN_FLAG stage=LEG2_BEFORE_LEG1_BREAK
+FP_LEVEL19_HOOK tf=M1 L=34 hook=... polarity=HOOK+ node=N2 latestHi=... latestLo=...
+```
+
+Audit must be compact enough to avoid destroying MT5 logs.
+
+---
+
+## 24. Relationship to future entry design
+
+Level 19 is the first bridge from anatomy to entry, but it does not create entries.
+
+It prepares future entry work by storing:
+
+```text
+where each timeframe is inside Rally View
+where each timeframe is inside Hook View
+which F has been established
+which probable F stage is forming next
+which hooks/nodes define the current structural position
+which sequence IDs and event IDs are responsible for the state
+```
+
+Future entry layers may read this state, but Level 19 itself must remain decision-neutral.
+
+Forbidden labels in Level 19:
+
+```text
+BUY
+SELL
+ENTRY_ALLOWED
+ENTRY_FORBIDDEN
+TAKE_PROFIT
+STOP_LOSS
+SIGNAL
+```
+
+Allowed labels:
+
+```text
+state labels
+sequence labels
+F stage labels
+Hook node labels
+scale labels
+source IDs
+```
+
+---
+
+## 25. Acceptance criteria
+
+Level 19 is accepted only if all conditions pass:
+
+```text
+1. Node/Hook/F-count outputs are not changed.
+2. Existing renderer output is not changed.
+3. Existing export files still work.
+4. Three timeframe inputs exist and default to M1/M10/H1.
+5. State updates on closed bars only.
+6. State is stored even when dashboard is disabled/minimized.
+7. Dashboard appears top-right by default and can be minimized.
+8. Rally View shows latest established F and probable next F stage up to F3.
+9. Hook View lists relevant hooks across scale L and shows hook polarity and current node status.
+10. CSV export exists for summary, rally rows, hook rows, and manifest.
+11. Static QA passes.
+12. MetaEditor compile passes.
+13. A visual smoke test confirms that panel rows match the existing Phoenix chart anatomy.
+```
+
+---
+
+## 26. Design summary
+
+Level 19 is the live market anatomy state map.
+
+It answers:
+
+```text
+Where are we now?
+Across which timeframes?
+From Rally View, where are we in F anatomy?
+From Hook View, where are we in Hook/ND/node anatomy?
+Which sequences and IDs are responsible for that state?
+```
+
+It does not answer:
+
+```text
+Should we enter?
+Where should we enter?
+Where should we exit?
+```
+
+That separation is intentional. The State Gate stores the map. Entry design comes later.
